      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "A roof in Utah generally lasts between 15 and 30 years for standard asphalt shingles, while metal or tile roofs can last 40 to 70 years or more .",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "between 15 and 30 years for standard asphalt shingles, while metal or tile roofs can last 40 to 70 years or more"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Lifespan by Roofing Material"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "3-Tab Asphalt Shingles: 15 to 20 years (thinner, more prone to wind and UV damage)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Architectural/Dimensional Shingles: 20 to 30 years (thicker and more durable against severe weather)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Impact-Resistant Shingles: 30 to 40 years."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roofing (Standing Seam/Steel): 40 to 70 years (sheds heavy snow and resists intense sun)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Tile or Slate Roofing: 50 to 100+ years."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Why Utah's Climate Ages Roofs Faster"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Intense UV Radiation: High elevations mean stronger sun exposure, which bakes and dries out asphalt shingles."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Extreme Temperature Swings: Rapid shifts from freezing nights to warm days crack and warp materials."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Heavy Snow and Ice Dams: Accumulation and melting cycles stress the roof structure and water-proof barriers."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "High Winds: Mountain gusts can lift, tear, or loosen edges."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "You can read more about local recommendations through guides like the Utah Roof Replacement Guide from Homer Roofing.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Utah Roof Replacement Guide",
            "link": "https://homerroofing.net/learning-center/roof-replacement-guide/"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What is your current roof made of?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "How old is the roof right now?"
          }
        ]
      },
